     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi D-Ruggies,<div><br></div><div>Just a quick note, we&#39;ve updated the D-RUG website, and it now includes the <a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2019/Taylor-Reiter-reproducible-examples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2019/Taylor-Reiter-reproducible-examples&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466168546000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Kiq_9cpcnIBpl5bHSw58O\">screencast of Taylor&#39;s presentation on reprex</a> (reproducible examples). Take a look if you missed it! There are some good points and discussion to consider as you think about posting/asking a question.</div><div><br></div><div>Next week (Tues Feb 5) I&#39;ll be giving a little demo of the <a href=\"https://github.com/ryanpeek/aggiedown\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/ryanpeek/aggiedown&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466168546000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3iMbOD_LFnCI8SSUcI7WsZ\">aggiedown package</a>, and how you might use it to write your dissertation/thesis (or a manuscript) in Rmarkdown, which can then be rendered to a lovely well formatted pdf. Mainly if you are interested in learning more about what you can do with Rmarkdown, <a href=\"https://bookdown.org/yihui/bookdown/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bookdown.org/yihui/bookdown/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466168546000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0QK2PCbU6oFA9UvSD61RuW\">bookdown</a>, come check it out. We&#39;ll screen cast as usual.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks and happy coding,</div><div><br></div><div>Adios,<br>Ryan</div><div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself, we find it hitched to everything else in the universe.&quot;<b><br>John Muir (My First Summer in the Sierra, 1911)</b></i></font></div><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b>-----------------------------------------------------</b></i></font></span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:19px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><div>Rya